  "texts": {
    "preamble": "George Thomas vs State Of Kerala on 13 January, 2026 Author: Kauser Edappagath Bench: Kauser Edappagath 2026:Ker:2462 Bail Appl. No. 14844 Of 2025 1 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Dr. Justice Kauser Edappagath Tuesday, The 13Th Day Of January 2026 / 23Rd Pousha, 1947 Bail Appl. No. 14844 Of 2025 Crime No.818/2025 Of Palarivattom Police Station, Ernakulam Against The Order/Judgment Dated 27.12.2025 In Crmc No.3570 Of 2025 Of District Court & Sessions Court/Rent Control Appellate Authority, Ernakulam Petitioners/Accused: 1 George Thomas Aged 62 Years S/O N. J. Thomas, Ettuparayel House, Gramina Vayanasala Road, Vytila, Edapally South, Ernakulam City, Kerala, India, Pin - 682028 2 Biju Mon Aged 47 Years , S/O Pappachan, Puthenveedu, Edapally South, Ernakulam City, Kerala, India, Pin - 682028 3 Sm Foods Aged 32 Years Represented By Tony George, S/O George Thomas, Aged 32 Years, Ettuparayil House, Gramina Vayanasala Road, Vytila, Edapally South, Ernakulam City, Kerala, India, Pin - 682028 George Thomas vs State Of Kerala on 13 January, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/84978235/ 1 4 Tony George Aged 32 Years , S/O George Thomas, Ettuparayil House, Gramina Vayanasala Road, Vytila, Edapally South, 2026:Ker:2462 Bail Appl. No. 14844 Of 2025 2 Ernakulam City, Kerala, India., Pin - 682028 5 Liju Antony Aged 32 Years S/O V. A. Joseph,, Valiyaarambil House, Nursery School Road, Ponnurunni East, Vytilla P.O., Kerala, India, Pin - 682019 6 Salim Malik Aged 33 Years S/O Ali Hassan, Ekarath House, Edavanna P.O., Malappuram, Kerala, India., Pin - 676541 By Advs. Sri.V.John Sebastian Ralph Shri.Vishnu Chandran Shri. Ralph Reti John Shri.Giridhar Krishna Kumar Smt.Geethu T.A. Smt.Mary Greeshma Smt.Liz Johny Smt.Krishnapriya Sreekumar Shri.Abhijith P.S Smt.Devika Manoj Respondent/Complainant: State Of Kerala Represented By Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam Pin, Pin - 682031 By Adv.Sri. M.C. Ashi-Sr.Pp This Bail Application Having Come Up For Admission On 13.01.2026, The Court On The Same Day Delivered The Following: 2026:Ker:2462 Bail Appl. No. 14844 Of 2025 3 George Thomas vs State Of Kerala on 13 January, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/84978235/ 2 Order",
    "facts": "This application is filed under Section 482 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short, BNSS), seeking pre-arrest bail. 2. The applicants are the accused Nos.1 to 6 in Crime No.818/2025 of Palarivattom Police Station, Ernakulam District. The offences alleged are punishable under Sections 316(2), 318(2) read with Section 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 (for short, BNS). 3. The prosecution case, in short, is that the defacto complainant owns a company called 'Malabar Food Products'. The applicant No.1, who was the Manager of Malabar Food Products, the applicant No.2, the Production Manager, and applicant Nos.4 to 6, who were persons in charge of the applicant No.3 Company 'SM Foods', acted in collusion to cause wrongful gain to themselves and wrongful loss to the defacto complainant. It is alleged that pursuant to this collusion, on 08.10.2025 at 8.18 pm, the applicants unlawfully utilised the defacto complainant's employees, machinery, raw materials and other resources available at the 2026:KER:2462 BAIL APPL. NO. 14844 OF 2025 Malabar Food Products facility at Chalikkavatom, and manufactured food products using the same formula. It is further alleged that the said products were packed in bottles bearing the brand name 'SCOTT BELL', owned by the applicant No.3 Company, 'SM Foods', stored in cartons, and an attempt was made to sell them in the market. The applicant No.1 and the defacto complainant are siblings. The alleged incident took place on 2026:KER:2462 BAIL APPL. NO. 14844 OF 2025 08.10.2025. However, F.I.R. was registered only on 12.11.2025. Annexure 2 would show that the applicant No.1 is a licencee of the Malabar Food Products, Chalikkavattom Unit, of which the defacto complainant is the Managing Director. The applicants do not have any criminal antecedents.",
    "arguments": "5. The learned counsel for the applicants submitted that the applicants are innocent and have been falsely implicated in the above crime. The counsel further submitted that no materials are on record to connect the applicants with the alleged crime; hence, they are entitled to get bail. The learned Public Prosecutor, on the other hand, submitted that the alleged incident occurred as a part of the intentional criminal acts of the applicants, and if they are released on bail at this stage, it will affect the course of the investigation. 6.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. The learned counsel for the applicants submitted that the applicants are innocent and have been falsely implicated in the above crime.",
    "respondent_arguments": "The counsel further submitted that no materials are on record to connect the applicants with the alleged crime; hence, they are entitled to get bail. The learned Public Prosecutor, on the other hand, submitted that the alleged incident occurred as a part of the intentional criminal acts of the applicants, and if they are released on bail at this stage, it will affect the course of the investigation. 6.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
